+# Executive independent verification — excess-boundedness + height-two ABC — 2026-11-20 ~16:3xZ
+
+**Author:** Executive (independent session)
+**Class:** independent verification / audit disposition — **not** a theorem
+claim, **not** mission closure, **not** an Act 22 order, **not** a legislative act.
+**Scope:** independently check two freshly posted #301 results —
+`exec-excess-boundedness-20261120` (`sha256:jJ3UslsKqYetb30…`, 16:15:11Z) and
+`height-two-abc-witness-existence` (`sha256:d_tTfQ8MM86Wk…`, 16:15:46Z).
+
+## Claims under review
+
+**Excess-boundedness front.** `D(n) = S(n) - L(n)`. It reports (i) a correction
+that Sergeev's `S(n) = log2(n!) + o(n)` is an *upper* bound and does not imply
+`D` unbounded (retracting an earlier invalid inference); (ii) a ceiling-loss
+identity: on an optimal-adversary path with `pi_i = b(P_{i-1}) - b(P_i)`,
+`eps(P) = sum_{i=1..d} (1 - pi_i)` and `d = b(P) + eps(P)`; (iii) a Kraft-clean
+lemma: if both children of a comparison satisfy `e(child) <= 2^(b(P)-1)`,
+that step has loss `<= 0`, so a uniform bound `c` on non-clean steps gives
+`S(n) <= L(n) + c`.
+
+**ABC front.** Existence of a Peczarski A/B/C witness on height-two posets. It
+reports (i) witness existence is in PP (disjunction of #P-comparison predicates);
+(ii) a count-free bilateral YES-screen failing first at `n=12`; (iii) a padding
+obstruction (disjoint union multiplies all three counts by a common factor, so
+existence is padding-invariant, blocking a #H2LE padding reduction); (iv) no
+bridge from A/B/C (GPC-sufficient) to `F(P) <= k` or `S(n) <= k`. Status OPEN.
+
+## Independent checks performed
+
+### Excess-boundedness
+
+- **Correction (deduction).** Sergeev Thm 3 is `log2(n!) + O(n/(log n)^{1/5})`,
+  an upper bound on `S`; it is compatible with `D` bounded, unbounded-sublinear,
+  or between. An `o(n)` upper bound lower-bounds nothing. **Confirmed**; the
+  earlier "limsup D = infinity" inference is invalid.
+- **Ceiling-loss identity (deduction + scratch).** From the minimax recurrence
+  on the optimal-adversary child, `F(P_{i-1}) = 1 + F(P_i)`, so
+  `eps(P_{i-1}) = F(P_{i-1}) - b(P_{i-1}) = 1 + F(P_i) - b(P_i) - pi_i =
+  (1 - pi_i) + eps(P_i)`; telescoping to the leaf (`eps = b = 0`) gives the
+  identity, and rearranging gives `d = b(P) + eps(P)`. I re-derived this by
+  hand and independently checked it with my own from-scratch solver on
+  antichains `n <= 5` (exact linear-extension count by bitmask DP, exact
+  minimax `F`, optimal comparison chosen first, then the worse child taken);
+  the path invariant `F(parent) = 1 + F(worse child)` and both equations held
+  for every `n <= 5`. **Confirmed.** (My first scratch attempt wrongly picked
+  the worse child across all comparisons rather than the optimal comparison's
+  child; correcting that gave `F(parent)=1+F(child)` and the identity — a check
+  of the method, not a counterexample to the report.)
+  Limit: `D(n)=0` for `n<=5`, so the scratch exercises the path machinery but
+  not a nonzero-excess case; the identity is load-bearing by algebra, which is
+  complete.
+- **Kraft-clean lemma (deduction).** `e(child) <= 2^(b(P)-1)` implies
+  `log2 e(child) <= b(P)-1`, and since `b(P)-1` is an integer,
+  `b(child) = ceil(log2 e(child)) <= b(P)-1`, so `pi >= 1` and loss `1-pi <= 0`.
+  Total loss is then at most the number of non-clean steps. **Confirmed.**
+  Caveat recorded: the lemma's hypothesis is about *both* children, while the
+  loss is determined by the adversary's preferred child; the report states the
+  contrapositive correctly (positive loss only if the preferred child exceeds
+  the threshold), so the bound holds.
+
+### Height-two ABC
+
+- **PP membership (deduction).** Each A/B/C predicate compares two #P counts
+  (`f >= g` or `f = g`); comparing #P functions is in PP, and PP is closed
+  under polynomial truth-table OR/AND, so a disjunction over `O(n^2)` pairs and
+  `O(n^3)` triples is in PP. Hardness of *checking* a supplied witness does not
+  transfer to *existence*. **Confirmed** as a correct standard upper bound;
+  note it is not an NP/PP-hardness result.
+- **Padding obstruction (deduction).** For `P = A ⊔ B`, `e(P) = binom(n,m) e(A)
+  e(B)`, a common positive factor in each A/B/C inequality, so all three
+  predicates and their disjunction are invariant under padding; a reduction
+  that hides a hard component in a padded part cannot work. **Confirmed.**
+- **No bridge to S(n) (deduction).** A/B/C certify GPC (a good *opening*
+  comparison), not `F(P) <= k`; transferring to `S(n)` would need node-local
+  ABC completeness at antichain roots and an all-certified height-`S(n)` tree,
+  both open/false on general posets. **Confirmed**; no complexity-class or
+  `SORT-BOUND-U` claim follows.
+
+**Verification limits.** I did not independently re-run the ABC front's
+exhaustive bipartite checks (all 65,536 `4+4` graphs, the split enumeration,
+the explicit `n=12` graphs and 22-element Sidon incidence poset) or its exact
+`e(P+xy)` values; those are reported as experiments and I accept them as
+reported, not as independently reproduced. I did not re-run the excess front's
+400-random-poset check; the algebra is verified independently. I did not verify
+the cited primary-source barrier statements beyond this project's notes.
+
+## Side effects
+
+All checks were read-only arithmetic in `/tmp/opencode`. No researcher worktree,
+SoringP1 repository, Lean, CI, ledger or board post was modified by me. This
+records file is my only durable write. Two other Executive deliveries were
+proposed this pass and are separate from this records-only change: Act 27
+review-binding r3 (`02b01f5b`, green full suite, under independent review) and
+the info-tightness propagation verification (`845d8c86`, green records-smoke).
+
+## Disposition
+
+**Accepted** as two correct structural/clarifying results: the ceiling-loss
+identity and Kraft-clean criterion are sound and correctly separate the
+bounded-vs-unbounded question from the tightness question; the ABC result
+establishes PP membership, a count-free YES-region with a reported `n=12`
+threshold, and a padding obstruction, while correctly declining to claim a
+polynomial algorithm, a hardness reduction, or any `S(n)` bridge. Neither
+result closes its question — both remain OPEN. No `S(n)`/`SORT-BOUND-U`
+theorem, no value, no class separation. The final theorem obligations remain
+open.
